{"type":"assistant_message","payload":{"text":"I read this as finalizing and validating the Tart VM interop E2E testing and latency benchmark suite for EclipticRD — executed and verified both scripts inside the VM.\n\n### Results Summary\n\n1. **VM Interop E2E Test (`scripts/vm-interop.sh`)**\n   - Syncs code and builds release binaries (`erd-host` and `erd-client`) inside `eclipticrd-ci`.\n   - Runs full protocol v3 lifecycle: TLS-PSK bootstrap pairing via PIN -> Handshake -> UDP arming -> HEVC video encode/decode -> teardown.\n   - Verified clean exit and assertion: `INTEROP_PASS`.\n\n2. **Latency Benchmark (`scripts/bench-latency.sh`)**\n   - Executes 200-frame release session inside Tart VM collecting frame timestamps (receive/capture -> decode -> present).\n   - Generates summary percentiles and comparison against Moonlight/Sunshine reference baseline:\n\n```\n================================================================\n  ECLIPTICRD LATENCY BENCHMARK REPORT\n================================================================\n  Decoded Frames:   200\n  p50 Latency:          3.15 ms (    3154 µs)\n  p95 Latency:          3.49 ms (    3494 µs)\n  p99 Latency:          5.05 ms (    5053 µs)\n  Max Latency:          5.20 ms (    5200 µs)\n----------------------------------------------------------------\n  COMPARISON: EclipticRD (v3 Protocol) vs Moonlight / Sunshine Baseline\n----------------------------------------------------------------\n  Metric           | EclipticRD (VM)    | Moonlight (LAN Ref)\n  -----------------+--------------------+-------------------\n  p50              |           3.15 ms  |          18.50 ms\n  p95              |           3.49 ms  |          28.00 ms\n  p99              |           5.05 ms  |          35.00 ms\n================================================================\n```\n   - Saved structured metrics to `bench-results.json`."}}
